## 4. THE INHERITANCE OF THE BINARY

### 4.1 The Descent of the Binary

The binary structure descends through the sequence:

| Stage | Binary | Source |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Morals | Helpful/Destructive | Survival imperative |
| Ethics | Good/Evil | Formalized morals |
| Spirituality | Hope/Despair | Response to uncertainty |
| Religion | Sacred/Profane | Formalized spirituality |
| Logic | True/False | Formalized ethics |

**The binary is inherited, not discovered.**

### 4.2 The Formal Inheritance

The inheritance is formal:

```
Moral Binary (Helpful/Destructive)
    ↓ (Abstraction)
Ethical Binary (Good/Evil)
    ↓ (Abstraction)
Spiritual Binary (Hope/Despair)
    ↓ (Abstraction)
Religious Binary (Sacred/Profane)
    ↓ (Abstraction)
Logical Binary (True/False)
```

Each abstraction:
- Removes context
- Generalizes application
- Preserves binary structure
- Loses original grounding

### 4.3 The Evidence in Language

Language preserves the inheritance:

| Term | Original | Derived |
|------|----------|---------|
| "Good" | Helpful (survival) | Moral approval |
| "Evil" | Destructive (survival) | Moral disapproval |
| "Right" | Straight, correct | Moral correctness |
| "Wrong" | Crooked, incorrect | Moral incorrectness |
| "True" | Faithful, trustworthy | Correspondence |
| "False" | Deceitful, untrustworthy | Non-correspondence |

**The language of logic is borrowed from ethics.**

**Formal:**

```
∀x (LogicalTerm(x) → Inherited(EthicalTerm(x)))
```

