A4: ∀x (Religion(x) → Formalization(Spirituality, x))
A5: ∀x (Logic(x) → Derived(Ethics, x))
```

### 6.2 The Inheritance Theorems

**Theorem 1: Morals Precede Ethics**

```
∀x (Ethics(x) → Precedes(Morals, Ethics))
∀x (Ethics(x) → Depend(Morals, Ethics))
```

**Proof:**

| Step | Statement | Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Ethics formalizes shared moral values | Axiom 2 |
| 2 | Formalization requires something to formalize | Definition |
| 3 | That which is formalized precedes the formalization | Definition |
| 4 | Therefore, morals precede ethics | From 1-3 |

**Theorem 2: Ethics Precedes Logic**

```
∀x (Logic(x) → Precedes(Ethics, Logic))
∀x (Logic(x) → Depend(Ethics, Logic))
```

**Proof:**

| Step | Statement | Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Logic is derived from ethics | Axiom 5 |
| 2 | Derivation presupposes the derived | Definition |
| 3 | That which is derived from precedes the derivation | Definition |
| 4 | Therefore, ethics precedes logic | From 1-3 |

**Theorem 3: The Binary Is Inherited**

```
∀x (Binary(x) → Inherited(Morals, x))
```

**Proof:**

| Step | Statement | Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Morals are the source of the original binary | Axiom 1 |
| 2 | Ethics inherits from morals | Axiom 2 |
| 3 | Logic inherits from ethics | Axiom 5 |
| 4 | The binary is transmitted through inheritance | Definition |
| 5 | Therefore, the binary is inherited from morals | From 1-4 |

